# assets/demo.tape — the README hero, hand-authored for THIS repo.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every other repo's tape is GENERATED by dotfiles-core's scripts/gen-hero-tape.sh from
# one shared zsh template. This one cannot be: the host layer here is PowerShell and the
# repo vendors no core/, so there is no zsh to `Set Shell`, no ~/.config/zsh/.zshrc to
# source and no `_core_cap` to type (dotfiles-core assets/hero-repos.txt says why the row
# is deliberately absent). The SHAPE is the shared one — the same font, size, palette,
# framerate and beat rhythm, the same three marquee moments, then this repo's own two —
# so the ten heroes read as one family. Keep it that way when you edit.
#
# Render (assets/README.md has the full recipe): from a WSL distro, with a `pwsh` shim on
# PATH that execs the Windows pwsh.exe through interop, `vhs assets/demo.tape`, then the
# gifsicle pass, and commit the gif WITH any tape change.

Output assets/demo.gif

Set Shell "pwsh"
Set FontFamily "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font"   # must be a Nerd Font, or the eza/starship icons break
Set FontSize 20
Set Width 1200
Set Height 700
Set Padding 20
Set Theme { "name": "Tokyo Night storm (dotfiles-core)", "background": "#24283b", "foreground": "#c0caf5", "selection": "#2e3c64", "cursor": "#c0caf5", "black": "#1d202f", "red": "#f7768e", "green": "#9ece6a", "yellow": "#e0af68", "blue": "#7aa2f7", "magenta": "#bb9af7", "cyan": "#7dcfff", "white": "#a9b1d6", "brightBlack": "#414868", "brightRed": "#db4b4b", "brightGreen": "#9ece6a", "brightYellow": "#e0af68", "brightBlue": "#7aa2f7", "brightMagenta": "#bb9af7", "brightCyan": "#7dcfff", "brightWhite": "#c0caf5" }
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
# 24, not vhs's 50: the frame count is the cost of a gif, not its length, and a terminal
# needs half that — the same reasoning as dotfiles-core assets/hero.tape.in.
Set Framerate 24

# --- silent setup: land on a clean prompt, with nothing that can attach or page ---
# vhs starts pwsh with -NoProfile and its own one-character prompt, so the profile is
# dot-sourced HERE — after the knobs the profile reads at load time are in place:
#   PSMUX_NO_AUTOLAUNCH   the Windows twin of Core's DOTFILES_NO_AUTOTMUX. powershell/os/
#                         30-windows.ps1 attaches psmux for any interactive shell, and the
#                         one vhs drives IS one — without this the tour is typed into a
#                         psmux pane, the same way dotfiles-core's first #877 render landed
#                         in tmux.
#   DOTFILES_UPDATE_CHECK the once-a-day update nudge (powershell/core/15-update.ps1),
#                         which would print a line the tour did not type.
#   GIT_PAGER=cat         glog would otherwise open less.
# PSReadLine's history predictions are switched off after the profile sets them up, so no
# ghost text from past sessions paints under the keystrokes. The `cd` exits on a wrong box
# rather than filming $HOME (dotfiles-core#698's defect), and `$IsWindows` is the host
# guard: a pwsh that is not Windows' has no scoop, no winget and none of this profile.
Hide
Type "$env:PSMUX_NO_AUTOLAUNCH='1'; $env:DOTFILES_UPDATE_CHECK='0'; $env:GIT_PAGER='cat'" Enter
Type "if (-not $IsWindows) { exit 1 }" Enter
Type ". $PROFILE" Enter
Type "Set-PSReadLineOption -PredictionSource None" Enter
Type "cd ~\code\dotgibson\dotfiles-Windows; if (-not (Test-Path .\task.ps1)) { exit 1 }" Enter
Type "clear" Enter
Show
Sleep 1500ms

# --- the tour: the three shared marquee moments, then the two that are this repo's ---
Type "ll" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 1600ms             # eza — icons + git status
Type "cat README.md" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 1600ms  # bat — syntax highlighting
Type "glog -8" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 1600ms        # git log, graphed and decorated
# The signature command is the fleet's: the same three characters every sibling types,
# resolving here to scoop + winget instead of dnf, pacman, apk, emerge, zypper or brew
# (powershell/core/15-update.ps1). It is the one step that does WORK — both managers refresh
# their sources before answering, ~7 s on this host — so it gets the long hold, the way
# dotfiles-core's registry gives Gentoo's `emerge --pretend` one.
Type "up -n" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 9s              # one verb → scoop status + winget upgrade
Type "core-version" Sleep 400ms Enter Sleep 2200ms   # the provenance line, as on every box
Sleep 1s
